  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member, I want to see in my MP list which conversations my correspondent has not read yet, as the forum and the legacy app show them, so that I know whether my last message was read. Operator report after a device test, 2026-11-07, milestone M4 (parity).\n\n### Verified\n- **HFR** marks it per row with `<span class=\"red\" title=\"Ce message n'a pas été lu par : <pseudos>\">[non lu]</span>` before the title. It means the **other party** has not read the conversation. This state is independent of one's own unread icon (`closedbp.gif`). Sources: HFR-PROTOCOL §6b `:149`, `:297`, `:508`, captures `R13a`, `R13b`, `R13u1`, `R123a`, `R123f`. In a group MP the tooltip names every member who has not read it yet, in lower case.\n- **The engine already parses it.** `PrivateMessageListParser.swift:37, 61-62` fills `PrivateMessageThread.unreadBy` and `isUnreadByOthers`, defined in `HFRModels/Lists/PrivateMessageThread.swift:10-14`.\n- **The app never displays it.** `MessageRowView.swift` shows only one's own unread state (dot, semibold). The bug is display-only.\n- **Legacy** showed a \"non lu\" capsule: `MPListView.swift:425-436` @ 2440d79, white caption on `systemGray`, 50 % opacity when the thread is viewed. GAP-111 records the capsule as not ported. This issue restores it.\n\n### Fix\n- In `MessageRowView`, when `thread.isUnreadByOthers` is true, show a small \"non lu\" capsule next to the title or the date, as legacy did.\n  - Accessibility label: \"Non lu par <pseudos>\", or \"Non lu par le destinataire\" when `unreadBy` is empty.\n  - Group MP: list the names from `unreadBy`.\n- Keep it visually distinct from one's own unread state (the dot and the #570 tint). Two states can be shown at once (`R13u1`).\n- Update GAP-111.\n- Test: a row model with `isUnreadByOthers` shows the capsule and its label; one's own unread state alone does not.\n\n### Routing\nDone in the same PR as #570 (same file, `MessageRowView`), by `ext/francoisgn-ui-570`: Sonnet writes, Opus reviews.",
